course: dictionary
lesson: 15112
title: The saiga: a nose like a filter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A saiga is an animal, and it is a word you can picture. Read the words around it to build the picture. «The saiga grazed on the dry grass of the plains.» Grazed means it ate grass, and plains are wide, flat lands, so a saiga is an animal that lives on open grassland.
explain: «The saiga has a big, soft, drooping nose.» Drooping means hanging down, so this animal has a large nose that hangs low. «In winter, its nose warms the cold air it breathes in.» This tells you the nose works like a filter, changing the air before it goes in.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. "The ____ grazed on the dry grass of the plains" still makes sense with saiga, so it is a kind of animal. When you are not sure, use a dictionary to check.
fact: A saiga is a kind of antelope.
fact: Saigas live on the dry grassy plains of Central Asia.
fact: «The saiga has a big, soft, drooping nose.» Drooping means hanging down.
fact: Its nose works like a filter: it warms cold air in winter and keeps out dust in summer.
fact: Saigas are endangered, which means they are at risk of dying out, so people work to protect them.
exercise: «The saiga grazed on the dry grass of the plains.» What is a saiga? | A small wooden boat | A kind of plant | *A kind of antelope | A type of cloud
exercise: «In winter, its nose warms the cold air it breathes in.» What job does the saiga's nose do? | It makes loud noises like a horn | It turns grass into sugar | *It works like a filter, warming cold air | It helps the saiga swim fast
exercise: Where do saigas live? | The deep bottom of the ocean | *The dry grassy plains of Central Asia | The thick rainforests of South America | The frozen ice of the Arctic
test: «Many saigas died from disease and hunting, so they are now endangered.» Why are saigas endangered? | They grew too big to move | They only eat fish from rivers | Too much rain and snow | *Disease and hunting
test: «In summer, the saiga's nose keeps out the dust.» What does the nose do in summer? | *It keeps out dust | It turns the nose blue | It warms the cold air | It makes a whistling sound
exam: The saiga lives on wide, open steppe land. What does the word saiga mean? | A kind of tall grass | *An antelope with a big, soft, drooping nose | A town in Central Asia | A type of stormy weather
